{"name":"Pedestrian Red","hex":"#cc1122","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"pedestrian","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of or intended for those who are walking.","Ordinary, dull; everyday; unexceptional."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A walker; one who walks or goes on foot, especially as opposed to one who uses a vehicle.","An expert or professional walker or runner; one who performs feats of walking or running."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pedestrian"},{"term":"red","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The color of the setting sun, blood, and strawberries; the color which is evoked by the longest visible wavelengths (between about 625–740 nm), and a primary additive color.","A revolutionary socialist or (most commonly) a Communist;  a Bolshevik, a supporter of the Bolsheviks in the Russian Civil War."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a red hue.","Having an orange-brown or orange-blond colour; ginger."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/red"}],"entries":[{"title":"Pedestrian","blocks":[{"text":"A pedestrian is a person traveling on foot, by wheelchair or with other mobility aids. Streets and roads often have a designated footpath for pedestrian traffic, called the sidewalk in North American English, the pavement in British English, and the footpath in Australian, Indian and New Zealand English. There are also footpaths not associated with thoroughfares; these include rural paths and urban short cuts."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/97/CrossWalk_%285465840138%29.jpg/330px-CrossWalk_%285465840138%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pedestrian","wikidata":"Q221488"},{"title":"Red","blocks":[{"text":"Red is the color at the long wavelength end of the visible spectrum of light, next to orange and opposite violet. It has a dominant wavelength of approximately 625–750 nanometers. It is a primary color in the RGB color model and a secondary color in the CMYK color model, and is the complementary color of cyan. Reds range from the brilliant yellow-tinged scarlet and vermillion to bluish-red crimson, and vary in shade from the pale red pink to the dark red burgundy."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cf/Delicious_fresh_strawberries_%284735910403%29.jpg/330px-Delicious_fresh_strawberries_%284735910403%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Red","wikidata":"Q3142"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e0/Pedestre.JPG/500px-Pedestre.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e0/Pedestre.JPG/1280px-Pedestre.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e0/Pedestre.JPG/500px-Pedestre.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A sign in Belo Horizonte, Brazil, directing pedestrians to an overpass for safe crossing.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3APedestre.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6b/Colecci%C3%B3n_de_hombres_cruzando.JPG/500px-Colecci%C3%B3n_de_hombres_cruzando.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6b/Colecci%C3%B3n_de_hombres_cruzando.JPG/1280px-Colecci%C3%B3n_de_hombres_cruzando.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6b/Colecci%C3%B3n_de_hombres_cruzando.JPG/500px-Colecci%C3%B3n_de_hombres_cruzando.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Pedestrian signal in Santa Ana, California.","li